      "writtenOn": "2021-05-17T07:44:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is an allow list, so we don\u0027t have to update this list if any external repo changes\n\nOnly if a new directory with a new BUILD file (that we want to use) is added to these 5 places:\n\nbuild/bazel/...\nbuild/pesto/...\nexternal/bazelbuild-rules_android/...\nprebuilts/sdk/...\nprebuilts/clang/...\n\nSince adding new directories with new BUILD files (that we want to use) is a fairly rare event at the moment, I would prefer to revisit this later. \n\nIf we switch to prefix/recursive matching now, we would probably also need a way for child directories to opt out, because of \".\" being on the allow list (for $TOP/BUILD). Adding the opt out logic and then opting out every directory under . (and also maintaining that opt out list over time) seems as bad or worse than just keeping the current approach, IMO?",
      "parentUuid": "044fa3f5_3e17ecc7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 136,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 146,
        "endChar": 49
      },
